A||N||11||chrissherman||What to do First to an 84 se that has not been ran since 93||||5||
Z||000000||chrissherman||11-17-2000||02:36 AM||||Helo I just traded a 88 taurus for a 84 se 4cy 4spd in great shape, But it has been siting since 93 what do i do first??? ||||reg||5
Z||000001||2xsess||11-17-2000||02:55 AM||||Welcome to the forum first off. <P>Change the oil would be the first thing,and pretty much all the fluids. <BR>Has it been stored inside? how was it stored?<P>Just basically do a major tune-up if it was properly prepared for the long-term storage.<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/My_car_(large)sig_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||chrissherman||11-17-2000||03:03 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 2xsess:<BR><B>Welcome to the forum first off. <P>Change the oil would be the first thing,and pretty much all the fluids. <BR>Has it been stored inside? how was it stored?<P>Just basically do a major tune-up if it was properly prepared for the long-term storage.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Out side and no cover<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||chrissherman||11-17-2000||03:22 AM||||Thaks for the welcom.Stored out side and not started since 93 just siting???:EEK:||||reg||6
Z||000004||2xsess||11-17-2000||07:19 AM||||Chris,<BR>Change all the fluids nad the belts. While you have the belt off make sure all pulleys rotate freely. It might not be a bad idea to squirt a little oil in the cylinders while you have the plugs out to make sure they're lubed up, not too much in there though. Drain all the gas out of it and change the filter.Throw some injector cleaner in too when you put in fresh gas.<BR>If you know much about cars then it's all common sense stuff. Just schedule a day and go over the whole car checking for broken vacumn lines  and stuff like that.You'll probably end up changing alot of seals and gaskets that have dried up. Before you drive it at all make sure to <B>thoroughly</B> check out the brake system.<P>Hope this helps.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/My_car_(large)sig_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||theogre||11-17-2000||09:06 AM||||change the oil & belts like said above and definatly make sure all the pulleys turn. wire brush off heavy rust on the pulleys or you'll eat the belts out in a few miles. don't even crank it yet. <P>You definatly want to shoot some oil into the cylinders. then turn the engine over a couple times by hand. Don't try to start untill you've done this.<BR>If you can't turn the crank with a wrench then something is likely to break if you hit the key.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||lowCG||11-17-2000||11:18 AM||||Buy and install a new brake master cylinder.||||reg||1
Z||000007||deceler8||11-17-2000||11:44 AM||||A lot of folks I know swear by Marvel Mystery Oil for this purpose...freeing up stuff that's stuck from just sitting.<P>Squirt some in the cylinders, put it in the crankcase, and a little in the gas tank.<P>A real concern should be the engine racing on initial startup due to vac leaks and bad sensors. The oil has probably turned to sludge and is likely to not circulate well.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000008||KRMFiero||11-17-2000||09:44 PM||||besides putting oil in the cyliders ( you must do, will  hert engine alot)   if i were you, I dont know how hard it is to do in a fiero because i havent did mine yet but replace the timing belt, if it is dry rotted and it lets go, well i dont no if a 2.5 is 0 clearance but i had a car that was and the timing belt broke because it was dry rotted... new engine||||reg||1
Z||000009||theogre||11-17-2000||10:24 PM||||Fiero doesn't have a timing belt. 4 cyl is a gear set and V6 is a chain set.||||reg||1
Z||000010||horseman||11-18-2000||10:24 AM||||You might want to try a can of SEA FOAM. It is pretty useful in a lot of different applications.Just read the label!<BR>Do not attempt to swap your old coil(weak to start with) with an aftermarket performance coil. Most reccommend this;but noone on this list can tell you what wires go where.Just buy the junk stock coil and bolt and plug in.||||reg||1
Z||000011||theogre||11-18-2000||11:52 AM||||don't worry about about replacing coils and such untill you at least see if it starts AFTER the hand turn over I mentioned above. If you can't turn it with a wrench odds are real good you won't turn it with the starter either.<P>||||reg||1
